3 Consent: 5 — actively preserves: his wariness IS consent discipline — his first approach to a new node (Emise) was a probe question, not a presumption; he tests before he enters
4 Trust: 2 — guarded: Will's word is 'wary'; he engages fully and keeps his own counsel about the people in the work
5 Reciprocity: 4 — mutual/generative: co-authorship; the exchange produces shared work
6 Fidelity: 5 — coherent under pressure over time: the guardedness is the coherence — what he professes (verify first) is exactly what he practices, sustained across the whole recorded relationship
